<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" dir="ltr">
<%- include('../partials/head') %>
<body class="portal-legal-body">
  <header class="portal-legal-header">
    <a href="/login" class="portal-legal-brand" aria-label="Findoly provider login">
      <img src="/images/findoly-logo.png" alt="Findoly">
      <span>Provider portal</span>
    </a>
    <a class="btn btn-light btn-sm" href="/login">Provider login</a>
  </header>

  <main class="portal-legal-shell">
    <article class="card portal-legal-card">
      <div class="card-body">
        <span class="portal-legal-kicker">Findoly Solutions LLP</span>
        <h1>Cancellation and Refund Policy</h1>
        <p class="portal-legal-lead">This policy applies to digital subscriptions and credits purchased through the Findoly Provider Portal.</p>
        <p class="portal-legal-effective">Effective date: 29 July 2026</p>
        <div class="portal-legal-content">

<section>
  <h2>1. Digital purchases</h2>
  <p>Findoly plans, subscriptions and credits are digital services. After a payment is verified, the applicable subscription or credits are activated in the provider account. No physical product is supplied.</p>
</section>
<section>
  <h2>2. Non-refundable purchases</h2>
  <p>All successfully purchased and activated digital subscriptions and credits are non-refundable. A completed purchase cannot be cancelled, returned, exchanged or converted into cash after activation.</p>
</section>
<section>
  <h2>3. Unused credits</h2>
  <p>Unused or partially used credits do not create a right to a refund. Credit validity, plan validity and any expiry information shown at purchase or in the Provider Portal continue to apply.</p>
</section>
<section>
  <h2>4. Payment or activation issue</h2>
  <p>If an amount is debited but the corresponding subscription or credits are not visible after payment verification, email <a href="mailto:<%= supportEmail %>"><%= supportEmail %></a> with the registered provider mobile number, payment date, amount and payment reference. Findoly will investigate the payment and activation records and take the appropriate corrective action.</p>
</section>
<section>
  <h2>5. Failed or pending transactions</h2>
  <p>A failed, pending, reversed or incomplete payment does not activate credits. The final status may depend on confirmation from the payment gateway or banking network.</p>
</section>
<section>
  <h2>6. Contact</h2>
  <p>Refund-policy and payment-discrepancy questions must be submitted by email to <a href="mailto:<%= supportEmail %>"><%= supportEmail %></a>.</p>
</section>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <section class="portal-legal-navigation" aria-label="Policies and support">
      <strong>Policies and support</strong>
      <%- include('../partials/policy-links', { policyLinksClass: 'portal-policy-links' }) %>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="portal-legal-page-footer">
    <span>© <%= new Date().getFullYear() %> <%= legalEntityName %></span>
    <a href="mailto:<%= supportEmail %>"><%= supportEmail %></a>
  </footer>
</body>
</html>
